Z||000000||DrRodey||01-30-2001||03:13 PM||||As most of you will remember, I was rebuilding a Ford 302 in my livingroom to put into my Jeep.  Now comes the fun questions.  The time has come to decide what i want to do with it.   Here are my options...<P>1: Put it back together with all the same parts i took out of it, except bearings and gaskets ect.<P>2: Buy a stroker crank, longer I beams, but don't bore it. (use stock size pistons)  (the cylenders are just too nice to waste that much money)<P>3: Rocker cam, arms, pushrods, ect.<P>4: Both #2 and #3.  <P>This vehicle will be used mainly for pulling my Fieros around to shows ect.  It will also be used as a semi daily driver, and some minor offroading.  <P>Any other options would be appreciated as well.  I am trying to get the best engine for the money.  The more power the better but I don't need too much, it is a wrangler afterall.<P>Thanks..<P><P>------------------<BR>Hi... My names Dan, and i'm addicted to Fieros.<BR>'88 Formula CONVERTIBLE<BR>'85 Coupe<BR>AOL IM = drrodey<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://freepages.ugo.com/RodeysPlace/files/fieroPage.JPG">          <BR> <A HREF="http://freepages.ugo.com/RodeysPlace/HomePlace.html" TARGET=_blank>freepages.ugo.com/RodeysPlace/HomePlace.html</A>||||reg||5
Z||000001||2M4 Dale||01-30-2001||06:27 PM||||Trade the whole thing off for a small block Chevy......just kidding !<P>No really, if your bottom end is OK then just reassemble it and hop up the top end with cam and lifters, rockers, etc.<P>Get a RV profile cam...great bottom end and milage...."for towing"||||reg||1
Z||000002||DrRodey||01-31-2001||12:39 PM||||Any other opinions out there????<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||01-31-2001||12:53 PM||||Stroking the motor will give you a little more torque. Since you are using it to tow I would go this route. As for cam and rockers, Stroking it will increase the torque and the horsepower. You could save the money on the top half. Unless you really want max horsepower. If you build it up too much you may lose some gas mileage. Since it's a daily driver, I don't think you want the mileage to drop.<BR><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
